  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the sound wave travelling in ideal gases of $\\mathrm{He}, \\mathrm{CH}_4$, and $\\mathrm{CO}_2$. All the gases have the same ratio $\\frac{P}{\\rho}$, where $P$ is the pressure and $\\rho$ is the density. The ratio of the speed of sound through the gases $\\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{He}}: \\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{CH}_4}: \\mathrm{v}_{\\mathrm{CO}_2}$ is given by"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{5}}: \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}: \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{3}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}: \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{3}}: \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{5}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}: \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{3}}: \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{3}}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{3}}: \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}: \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{5}}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{v}_{\\text {sound }}=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\gamma \\mathrm{p}}{\\rho}} \\\\ & \\gamma=1+\\frac{2}{\\mathrm{f}} \\\\ & \\gamma_{\\mathrm{He}}=\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ & \\left.\\gamma_{\\mathrm{CH}_4}=\\gamma_{\\mathrm{CO}_2} \\approx 1.33=\\frac{4}{3} \\quad \\text { (Experimental data }\\right)\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}